Just as a quick bit of advice about Usenet etiquette: you probably want
to quote at least a bit of the post you're responding to (preferably
edited to show only the most memorable or relevant parts), and before
your own post. Usenet's quite a slow communication mechanism, and
conversations are unlikely to be fresh in people's mind when you
continue them; and although most people's newsreaders are capable of
finding the other posts in the conversation, it's still typically a pain
to switch back and forth from one post to another to follow the thread.
Having conversations self-contained makes life easier for everyone.

(Note to the people who are inevitably going to complain about
topicality: I'd rather explain this myself before a troll does it for
me, and in much less useful language.)

